-JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.
+JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed below.
+
+## Authentication and roles
+
+Every request requires `Authorization: Bearer <key>`, matched against
+`apiKeys` in the data file. Missing, malformed or unknown keys return 401
+(`unauthorized`); insufficient permissions return 403 (`forbidden`).
+
+Viewers may use GET routes except `/audit`. Cooks may also POST to
+`/recipes/:id/cook`, `/batches/:id/waste`, `/temperatures`, and
+`/stocktakes/:id/counts`. Managers may use every route, including starting
+and finishing stock-takes. Unrecognized roles have no permissions.
+
+Successful data-changing requests append an audit entry with `time` (ISO
+instant), `name` (key name), `method`, `path` (including query), and `status`.
+The audit entry and data change are saved together. Reads and rejected
+requests do not create audit entries. `GET /audit` returns an array newest
+first; equal times use reverse insertion order. Keys are never included.

